[ti:Day 06]

[00:00.00]subjugate 例 The problem is how to subjugate the rivals at a lower cost. 问题在于如何用较低的成本征服 对手。
[00:08.78]packing 例 The packing charge of this article is about 5% of its total cost. 这件商品的包装费用约占其 总成本的百分之五。
[00:18.03]carton 例 We hope that you will agree to our opinion and accept our carton packaging. 希望贵方能
[00:28.48]contaminate 例 We continually wage war on the insects, for they contaminate our food and carry diseases. 我们不断地同昆虫斗争，因为它们污染食物、传 播疾病。
[00:41.66]competition 例 Thei r goals have been to stimulate competition, promote efficiency and benefit consumers. 他们的目标是激励竞争、提升效率和 使消费者受益。
[00:55.30]monologue 例 He went into a monologue on his last day at the company. 在公司的最后一天，他滔滔不 绝地讲了很多话。
[01:03.63]consist 例 Most of these groups consist of graduate students and faculty, but some undergraduates join as well. 绝大多数的小组由 研究生和教职人员组成，但是也有些大学生加入 其中。
[01:17.72]grocery 例 He was employed in a local grocery store as a delivery boy. 他在当地的一家杂货店当送货 员。
[01:26.20]priority 例 The development of technology is a top priority of the company. 技术开发是该公司优先 考虑的事项。
[01:35.60]eligible 例 Anyone obtaining an MBA degree is eligible to apply for the position of manager in our company. 凡是获得了工商管理硕士学位的人，都 可以申请我们公司的经理职位。
[01:48.93]disorientate 例 I felt completely disorientated by the maze of streets. 弯弯曲曲的街道让我完全迷失了方 向。
[01:58.02]verbalise 例 He found it really hard to verbalise the concepts of this design. 他发现要描述清楚这个 设计的理念真的很难。 ex coupon (x.c.) 无息票
[02:07.72]buoyant 例 Some businesses have proved they are able to keep sales buoyant even in a tough market. 一些企业已经证明，即使市况趋紧，它们也有能 力保持旺盛的销售势头。
[02:19.84]assembly 例 The company hopes for some cost cuts after the installation of this new automated assembly line. 该公司希望在安装了新的自动装 配流水线之后能降低一部分成本。
[02:33.48]elaborate 例 We're here to elaborate our requirements for the trademark design. 我方是来详细阐述我 方对商标设计的要求的。
[02:43.63]commerce 例 Gates is not only outstanding in technology. What is more significant is that he gets through the crux passway between technology and commerce. 盖茨的杰出不仅体现在技术上， 更重要的是，他打通了技术和商业之间的关键通 道。
[03:03.32]hoard 例 The futures market does sometimes signal that prices are likely to rise, which might prompt speculators to hoard oil in anticipation. 期货市场有时确实会发出价格可能 上升的信号，这也许会促使投机者提前囤积石 油。
[03:21.35]inroad 例 The R&D team has made considerable inroad on this project. 研发小组已经在这个项目 上投入了不少资金。
[03:29.84]ingredient 例 Passion is a key ingredient in our work and life. 激情是我们工作与生活中的一个关键因素。
[03:37.57]clue 例 In an efficient market, past performance is not only no guarantee of future performance, it offers no clue whatsoever. 在有效市场中，过 去的业绩不仅不能为将来的业绩提供担保，甚至 连任何线索都提供不了。
[03:53.47]explore 例 The new market needs to be explored to gain a bigger market share. 不断探索新市场才 能获得更大的市场份额。
[04:02.87]destabilise 例 Any change in the food chain is likely to destabilise the entire ecosystem. 食物链的任何 改变都很可能破坏整个生态系统的稳定性。
[04:14.23]all-round 例 The enterprise has undertaken all-round technological renovation. 这个企业进行了全面 的技术改造。
[04:24.68]amass 例 If you want to amass money, your aim is to extinguish the competition, putting yourself in a position where you can set the price. 假如你 想赚钱，那么你就应该把消灭竞争、将自己置于 价格制定者的地位作为目标。
[04:41.81]backpedal 例 She later sought to backpedal by insisting that she has been to America before. 后来，她 试图打退堂鼓，一直坚持说她曾去过美国。
[04:53.32]consistent 例 There is a consistent thread running through all these policies. 所有这些政策中贯穿 着一条始终如一的主线。
[05:03.32]circular 例 Circular references are not always bad and, in fact, are sometimes absolutely necessary. 实际上，循环引用也不总是有害的，有时它绝对 是必需的。
[05:16.20]acceptance 例 There is often a certain lag between scientific invention and cultural acceptance. 科 学发明与文化接受之间经常会有一定的时间差。
[05:28.62]denomination 例 The dealings took place on the black market through unofficial gold traders in exchange for high denomination banknotes. 为 换取高面额钞票，这些交易都在黑市上通过非官 方的黄金交易商进行。
[05:46.20]complement 例 I believe you will come to complement them, though you do not want to duplicate efforts. 我相信你会出手帮助他们，尽管你并不想 做重复的工作。
[05:58.92]abolish 例 The association wanted to change the constitution to abolish direct elections to the presidency. 那个协会曾想要改变宪法，废除总统 直选制。
[06:12.71]identical 例 My opinion is not identical to his. 我的意见 与他的观点不同。
[06:18.62]distress 例 Business competitors always take advantage of each other's distress resulting from the economic downturn to increase their market share. 商业竞争对手之间总是利用对方经 济低迷时的亏空来提升市场份额。
[06:37.86]backpack 例 The tag on your backpack tells me what it is made of. 从你背包上的标签可以知道它是用什 么材料制造的。
[06:45.59]amend 例 Congress may amend the proposed tax bill. 议会可能会修正提议的税法。
[06:51.80]coherence 例 Successful expansions are about coherence as well as price. 成功的扩张是和连贯性及价格相 关的。
[07:01.04]inventory 例 To establish the product inventory, all the relative data and materials must be classified carefully. 为了建立产品库存目录，所有的相关数 据与材料必须仔细分类。
[07:15.74]forthcoming 例 Are there any new applications planned for design or development or implementation for the forthcoming year? 是否计划在即将到来的一 年里设计、开发或安装任何新应用程序？
[07:31.65]inconvertible 例 Foreign currency is inconvertible in this bank. 这家银行不能兑换外币。
[07:39.98]hypothesis 例 What would it mean for the efficient market hypothesis if the market rallied on the news? 如果市场因为这个消息而恢复，对有效市场假说 来说意味着什么呢？
[07:52.86]domestic 例 According to the investigation, low prices have crippled domestic output and foreign imports. 据调查，低物价已经阻碍了国内产出和 国外进口。
[08:06.49]falter 例 Will the economic miracle falter or even collapse? 这种经济奇迹会衰退甚至崩溃吗？
[08:14.07]quorum 例 The meeting was adjourned because there was insufficient quorum. 会议之所以延期是因为 没有达到法定人数。 unlisted securities 未上市证券
[08:23.61]mentor 例 The mentor needs the support of management. 这位顾问需要管理层的支持。
[08:30.28]upscale 例 The restaurant is well-known as an upscale restaurant for professionals. 那家饭店以质优价 高、服务专业而广为人知。
[08:41.04]eccentric 例 The femal manager is regarded as something of an eccentric. 那位女经理被认为个 性有点古怪。
[08:50.13]front-line 例 The value zone has naturally shifted to the frontier where front-line employees and customers interact. 自然而然地，价值区间已经 转移到一线员工和客户交互所在的前端了。
[09:05.28]ban 例 The trade of seal pelts and meat was curtailed by a 2012 Import Ban. 2012 年进口禁 令禁止进行海豹皮和海豹肉的交易。
[09:14.82]brunch 例 On Sundays, many Americans get up late and go out for brunch. 在周日，许多美国人都睡 到很晚，然后外出去吃早午餐。
[09:23.46]makeshift 例 This makeshift kiosk is on the outskirts of the city. 这个临时搭建的售货亭设在城市郊外。
[09:31.64]beneficial 例 He believes that the stability of actual and expected inflation of around 2% has been hugely beneficial to society. 他认为将实际通货 膨胀率和预期通货膨胀率的稳定性保持在2%左右 会对社会十分有利。
[09:48.00]altruistic 例 The public doubt whether several actors' motives for donating the money are altruistic. 公众怀疑一些演员的捐款动机是有私心的。
